from fastapi import FastAPI
from hermion.api.routes import synthesize, health

app = FastAPI(title="Hephaestus TTS Service - Hermion", version="1.0")

app.include_router(health.router, prefix="/api")
app.include_router(synthesize.router, prefix="/api")

@app.get("/")
def root():
    return {"message": "October 21, 2025, brings a mix of updates on various fronts, including law enforcement, infrastructure, and environmental concerns. The day begins with a focus on the aftermath of the recent earthquakes in Davao Oriental, where schools have resumed face-to-face classes after a suspension due to structural concerns. Meanwhile, a landslide in Bukidnon has prompted a search and rescue operation, with a temporary detour planned to ensure public safety.\n\n**Detailed Reports**\n\n1. **Davao City Police Office (DCPO) Arrests Suspects, Seizes Drugs**\nThe DCPO arrested 88 suspects and seized over P1.1 million worth of illegal drugs in a week-long crackdown. The operation resulted in the arrest of 42 suspects in 37 anti-drug operations, with 150.017 grams of shabu (estimated street value: P1,020,115.60) and 120.49 grams of marijuana (estimated street value: P97,015.20) confiscated.\n\n2. **Olanolan Vows to Fight On After Ombudsman Suspension Over Demolition Stand**\nBarangay 76-A chief Robert E. Olanolan has been suspended for one month without pay by the Office of the Ombudsman-Mindanao for his opposition to a demolition project in the Cabacan-Times Beach area. Olanolan attributes the suspension to his stance against the demolition, which he believes would displace long-time residents.\n\n3. **Trillanes Files Plunder Complaint vs. Duterte, Go Over P7-B Infrastructure Projects**\nFormer Senator Antonio Trillanes IV has filed a plunder complaint against former President Rodrigo Duterte, Senator Christopher \"Bong\" Go, and their family members over alleged anomalous infrastructure contracts worth billions of pesos.\n\n4. **Search for Couple in Bukidnon Landslide Continues; DPWH Plans 2-Week Detour**\nSearch and rescue operations for a couple feared buried under a massive landslide in Quezon, Bukidnon, continue. The Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) Technical Group has planned a two-week detour to construct a temporary road beside the collapsed section of the Bukidnon-Davao Road.\n\n5. **Olanolan Vows to Fight On After Ombudsman Suspension Over Demolition Stand**\nBarangay 76-A chief Robert E. Olanolan has been suspended for one month without pay by the Office of the Ombudsman-Mindanao for his opposition to a demolition project in the Cabacan-Times Beach area. Olanolan attributes the suspension to his stance against the demolition, which he believes would displace long-time residents.\n\n**Regional or Analytical Insight**\n\nThe news today highlights the ongoing challenges in Davao Oriental, where the recent earthquakes have left a lasting impact on the community. The resumption of face-to-face classes in schools is a positive step, but the need for structural safety assessments and inspections remains a pressing concern. The landslide in Bukidnon serves as a stark reminder of the risks associated with natural disasters and the importance of infrastructure development. The ongoing disputes over land use and demolition projects, such as the one in Cabacan-Times Beach, underscore the need for effective governance and community engagement. As the region continues to recover from these challenges, it is essential to prioritize the well-being and safety of its residents.\n\n**Insights**\n\nThe news today paints a picture of a region grappling with the aftermath of natural disasters and ongoing development challenges. The resumption of classes in schools and the search and rescue operation in Bukidnon demonstrate the efforts being made to address these issues. However, the suspension of Olanolan and the plunder complaint filed by Trillanes highlight the need for effective governance and accountability in the region. As the community continues to recover, it is crucial to prioritize the safety and well-being of its residents, while also addressing the underlying issues that contribute to these challenges."}
